      "problem": "Find the point where the line $9x-3y=7$ intersects the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation and solve for $y.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-3y & =7 \\\\ 9(0)-3y & =7 \\\\ -3y & =7 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the $y$-intercept is $-\\frac{7}{3}.$ Thus, the line intersects the $y$-axis at $(0,-\\frac{7}{3}).$",
